WEBVTT

00:06.987 --> 00:10.747
Y'know, you were the last guy 
I figured would bite the dust.

00:10.747 --> 00:13.317
It still doesn't feel real.

00:13.317 --> 00:16.897
He died shielding his son. 
He must be satisfied.

00:16.897 --> 00:18.217
You've got that right!

00:18.217 --> 00:21.707
But with Zenith in the state she's in?

00:21.707 --> 00:23.667
Better that than dead.

00:23.667 --> 00:28.397
Yes. Zenith must be happy, too, 
surrounded by family.

00:28.397 --> 00:30.987
And she has a son she can count on.

00:31.767 --> 00:33.167
Speak of the devil.

00:33.487 --> 00:35.367
Hey there, you two!

00:35.367 --> 00:37.467
Good morning to you all.

00:39.347 --> 00:41.137
You're leaving today, then?

00:41.427 --> 00:44.157
What's the matter, boss? Miss me already?

00:44.157 --> 00:46.187
Of course not.

00:46.187 --> 00:50.737
Well, it looks like things have settled 
down at your place, so it's time to go.

00:50.737 --> 00:54.927
We stayed longer than Paul 
deserved, if anything.

00:54.927 --> 00:58.077
Vierra and Shierra are long gone.

00:58.077 --> 01:01.267
You won't be attending my wedding, then?

01:01.267 --> 01:03.987
Ha! Who wants to celebrate 
a lecherous elf?

01:03.987 --> 01:05.427
What did you call me?!

01:06.167 --> 01:09.937
Stop, both of you! This isn't the time!

01:10.467 --> 01:12.497
I see some things never change.

01:12.497 --> 01:14.047
Oh, right. Boss.

01:14.467 --> 01:16.517
I almost forgot.

01:18.387 --> 01:19.887
What's this?

01:19.887 --> 01:23.317
Your share of the loot from 
the Teleporter Labyrinth.

01:23.317 --> 01:24.977
Wait. This is way too much.

01:26.607 --> 01:28.617
Paul's share's in there, too.

01:29.817 --> 01:33.227
Plus a little something from us.

01:33.647 --> 01:34.987
Geese...

01:34.987 --> 01:37.417
I told you, I'm fine with "new guy."

01:37.757 --> 01:40.857
You've got more mouths to feed now, right?

01:41.297 --> 01:43.907
Don't hold back. Just take it.

01:44.187 --> 01:46.547
And take good care of your family.

01:47.917 --> 01:48.927
I will!

02:30.727 --> 02:33.597
Mr. Greyrat. Thank you for the other day.

02:33.937 --> 02:36.537
Please give my best to little Aisha.

02:36.537 --> 02:38.597
Thank you. I'll be sure to.

03:10.097 --> 03:15.977
<b>III</b>

03:10.097 --> 03:15.977
<b><i>Mushoku Tensei</i></b>

03:10.097 --> 03:15.977
<b><b><i>Jobless Reincarnation</i></b></b>

03:19.247 --> 03:20.887
Oh, Big Brother.

03:20.887 --> 03:22.157
Welcome home.

03:22.157 --> 03:23.187
Good to be home.

03:23.187 --> 03:24.957
Did Sylphie already go out?

03:24.957 --> 03:27.957
She went to work right after you left.

03:27.957 --> 03:29.357
Oh.

03:29.357 --> 03:33.347
<i>Come to think of it, 
I don't bring in any money now, do I?</i>

03:33.677 --> 03:37.687
<i>How does it look for a husband to 
be unemployed when his wives work?</i>

03:39.117 --> 03:41.697
Aisha, when did Mom start doing that?

03:41.697 --> 03:45.527
Huh? Oh, a while back.

03:45.527 --> 03:50.667
My mom stopped her at first, 
but she helps me when I'm gardening.

03:50.667 --> 03:53.637
Lady Zenith is better at it than I am.

03:53.637 --> 03:54.877
Huh...

03:54.877 --> 03:57.807
Roxy, how many times are you 
going to make this mistake?!

03:57.807 --> 04:02.097
<i>Zenith took good care of the 
plants in our yard back in Buena.</i>

03:58.247 --> 04:02.097
I know you can put it right, but 
won't you stop to think how I feel?

04:02.097 --> 04:05.637
<i>Maybe that has something to 
do with how she's acting now.</i>

04:02.097 --> 04:05.637
In the first place, do you really need 
to use trees for target practice?

04:06.127 --> 04:11.357
<i>Anyway, it might bring her memories 
back, so I'd better leave her to it.</i>

04:12.867 --> 04:14.377
By the way, Aisha,

04:15.157 --> 04:18.517
you know you can call my mom "Mom," right?

04:18.517 --> 04:23.527
Nope. My mom says to call 
Lady Zenith "her ladyship."

04:23.527 --> 04:26.757
Lilia does? Talk about strict.

04:27.067 --> 04:28.597
<i>Well, why argue?</i>

04:28.597 --> 04:32.257
<i>What we call each other doesn't 
matter, as long as we're family.</i>

04:32.257 --> 04:36.127
<i>Besides, gardening together, 
they look just like mother and daughter.</i>

04:36.967 --> 04:38.627
Oh, Big Brother,

04:38.627 --> 04:40.137
you have today off, right?

04:40.137 --> 04:40.967
Yeah.

04:40.967 --> 04:42.437
In that case,

04:42.437 --> 04:44.437
come by my room later!

04:46.177 --> 04:49.967
Lucie-pie, Daddy's here.

04:49.967 --> 04:53.317
Bla-bla-blaargh!

04:55.827 --> 04:58.537
I just can't get her to laugh for me.

04:58.537 --> 05:01.947
She reminds me of you 
when you were little.

05:02.547 --> 05:08.407
His lordship often struggled to 
make you laugh, just like that.

05:08.717 --> 05:10.087
Did he really?

05:10.087 --> 05:12.407
<i>I guess maybe that did happen.</i>

05:19.087 --> 05:20.747
What could that be?

05:20.747 --> 05:22.537
I'll go see.

05:34.857 --> 05:37.327
Nothing wrong in Aisha's room.

05:38.657 --> 05:39.487
Who's there?!

05:57.167 --> 05:58.427
A treant?

06:02.347 --> 06:04.557
Why didn't you say something sooner?

06:04.557 --> 06:06.527
I was going to!

06:06.527 --> 06:09.977
But you were so busy that 
I thought it could wait!

06:09.977 --> 06:12.937
Then you found it before I could tell you!

06:14.187 --> 06:17.867
<i>Treants are the most common 
monsters in this world.</i>

06:17.867 --> 06:22.097
<i>You could say they're like 
slimes in a certain RPG.</i>

06:22.097 --> 06:23.077
<i>But...</i>

06:23.077 --> 06:25.837
Has it always been this active?

06:25.837 --> 06:28.487
No. It didn't move at all at first.

06:28.487 --> 06:32.077
Meaning something caused 
it to turn into a monster.

06:32.497 --> 06:34.817
Have you done anything unusual with it?

06:34.817 --> 06:38.577
Hm... I don't think so.

06:39.227 --> 06:44.187
Oh, but I do give it leftover 
bathwater sometimes.

06:44.887 --> 06:48.057
<i>Bathwater with Sylphie's and 
Aisha's sweat mixed in?!</i>

06:48.057 --> 06:52.307
<i>Of course! It makes sense that it 
sprouted gropey tentacles, then.</i>

06:52.307 --> 06:54.437
<i>Like hell it does!</i>

06:55.707 --> 07:00.017
Well, whatever the cause, we'd better 
get rid of it. Burn it or something.

07:00.017 --> 07:02.197
What?! But I worked so hard to grow it!

07:02.197 --> 07:04.467
What do you want to burn it for?!

07:04.467 --> 07:07.877
Aisha, this is a treant. A monster.

07:07.877 --> 07:10.417
But it's so small and cute!

07:10.417 --> 07:13.517
It may attack people when it 
gets bigger. It's dangerous.

07:13.517 --> 07:16.577
I'll train it so it won't hurt anyone!

07:17.877 --> 07:19.537
Please, Big Brother?

07:19.537 --> 07:20.907
Can't I keep it?

07:20.907 --> 07:22.397
Act as cute as you like, 
but the answer is no.

07:22.397 --> 07:25.037
But it hasn't done anything wrong.

07:25.037 --> 07:28.637
And it listens to me. Watch!

07:29.097 --> 07:30.197
Shake.

07:31.627 --> 07:32.807
See?

07:34.967 --> 07:37.397
Are you sure I can't keep it?

07:41.197 --> 07:42.147
I'm sure.

07:43.147 --> 07:44.337
Fine.

07:44.337 --> 07:47.987
If you really won't let me, 
I know just what I'll do.

07:48.497 --> 07:51.987
I'll tell Sylphie and 
Roxy about you-know-what.

07:51.987 --> 07:53.047
What do you mean?

07:53.357 --> 07:55.807
The secret room in the basement!

07:56.407 --> 07:58.237
<i>What?!</i>

07:58.527 --> 08:01.757
<i>Don't tell me she means the altar?!</i>

08:01.957 --> 08:05.567
A-Aisha, I'm only thinking of your safety—

08:04.847 --> 08:08.527
No freakiness you get up to will faze me,

08:08.527 --> 08:11.627
but what will Sylphie and Roxy think?

08:11.627 --> 08:18.137
Especially Roxy. How will she like you 
putting her old undies on a pedestal?

08:20.247 --> 08:21.877
<i>How could she?!</i>

08:21.877 --> 08:24.937
<i>Here I am, thinking of her safety, 
and she blackmails me?!</i>

08:24.937 --> 08:27.007
<i>Oh, damn it! What should I do?!</i>

08:27.007 --> 08:28.317
<i>What's my best move here?!</i>

08:28.317 --> 08:30.417
<i>Oh, goddess!</i>

08:30.417 --> 08:31.197
Um...

08:31.787 --> 08:34.197
I heard my name.

08:34.197 --> 08:37.467
Wh-What are you doing here? 
What about school?

08:37.467 --> 08:39.647
I forgot something at home.

08:40.997 --> 08:42.587
Listen, Roxy,

08:42.587 --> 08:44.427
my brother has your—

08:55.397 --> 08:56.807
A treant?

08:56.807 --> 08:58.957
Th-That's right, Roxy!

08:58.957 --> 09:01.687
Aisha is saying she wants to raise it!

09:01.687 --> 09:03.917
But that's too risky. 
I mean, it's a monster.

09:03.917 --> 09:06.367
Won't you tell her that 
it's a bad idea, too?

09:07.747 --> 09:09.247
I don't see a problem.

09:10.397 --> 09:14.017
Treants take to people 
if you raise them right,

09:14.017 --> 09:16.707
and I doubt it could harm 
anyone at this size.

09:16.707 --> 09:18.967
Y-You really think so?

09:18.967 --> 09:19.847
I do.

09:19.847 --> 09:23.617
The Migurd raise them to keep 
birds out of our fields.

09:23.997 --> 09:26.957
<i>Oh, yeah. Now that she mentions it...</i>

09:29.747 --> 09:30.887
Aisha,

09:31.207 --> 09:33.227
your brother was wrong.

09:33.577 --> 09:38.437
It's okay. I know you 
were just worried for me.

09:38.437 --> 09:40.607
Yes, of course I was.

09:42.127 --> 09:45.077
So, I won't mention you-know-what.

09:47.157 --> 09:49.447
You're the best!

09:52.677 --> 09:54.577
What brought this on?

09:55.467 --> 09:59.747
<i>And so, the treant became 
our latest family pet.</i>

10:00.057 --> 10:01.697
<i>It's name is Byt.</i>

10:01.947 --> 10:04.837
<i>Still, I can't believe 
she found the altar.</i>

10:04.837 --> 10:07.397
<i>It really doesn't pay 
to forget about maids.</i>

10:08.087 --> 10:09.297
Whoa!

10:09.617 --> 10:13.717
So, it can nullify barriers 
as well as ordinary spells.

10:14.177 --> 10:16.707
No wonder this crystal is legendary.

10:16.707 --> 10:19.777
Yes. We ought to study it in more detail.

10:19.777 --> 10:20.667
Yeah.

10:21.597 --> 10:27.617
<i>The technical name for the hydra scales 
I got from Geese is "absorptive manatite."</i>

10:28.077 --> 10:30.847
<i>Through experiments,</i>

10:30.847 --> 10:36.177
<i>we learned that it instantly breaks 
down things made of mana.</i>

10:36.567 --> 10:39.947
<i>That's a hell of a power, 
and it was a hell of an enemy.</i>

10:43.857 --> 10:46.297
How about we call it here for today?

10:46.297 --> 10:48.227
Couldn't we keep going a bit longer?

10:48.227 --> 10:51.717
I wouldn't mind, but what's the rush?

10:51.717 --> 10:54.707
I mean, it's not really urgent.

10:55.177 --> 10:56.217
Just...

10:56.557 --> 11:00.777
<i>Danger may threaten my 
family again someday.</i>

11:01.197 --> 11:06.107
<i>I figure it's better to do everything 
I can now to prepare.</i>

11:06.107 --> 11:09.367
<i>I don't want to lose anyone ever again.</i>

11:10.037 --> 11:11.447
Rudeus?

11:12.397 --> 11:13.367
Master!

11:13.727 --> 11:15.137
Forgive my tardiness!

11:15.137 --> 11:18.307
Zanoba Shirone has now arrived!

11:18.307 --> 11:19.407
Arrived!

11:19.407 --> 11:21.417
Arrived way too late.

11:21.417 --> 11:24.497
We told you we were experimenting 
with the absorptive manatite today.

11:24.497 --> 11:29.327
Oh, you know. I grew so engrossed in 
my research, I lost track of the time.

11:29.327 --> 11:31.927
Studying that automaton?

11:31.927 --> 11:33.247
How is that going?

11:33.247 --> 11:36.437
As to that, I disassembled 
its inner workings

11:36.437 --> 11:39.127
and discovered a large 
mana crystal at its core!

11:38.957 --> 11:41.767
O-Okay, just calm down.

11:39.127 --> 11:41.767
I assumed it was a single stone,

11:40.187 --> 11:41.667
Grand Master.

11:41.667 --> 11:43.067
I made this.

11:41.767 --> 11:43.007
but on further inspection,

11:43.007 --> 11:48.937
I found it to be made of many smaller 
crystals inscribed with magic circles!

11:43.067 --> 11:44.437
G-Great.

11:48.937 --> 11:52.777
This discovery could turn 
accepted wisdom on its head!

11:52.777 --> 11:55.787
What do you make of the 
fruits of Julie's training?!

11:55.787 --> 12:01.127
I may be biased, Master, but I believe 
it equals your own handiwork!

12:01.127 --> 12:02.797
Yes, it's well made.

12:02.797 --> 12:04.957
You think so as well, then?!

12:04.957 --> 12:06.337
Master!

12:06.667 --> 12:08.447
That's wonderful, Julie!

12:08.447 --> 12:11.567
Persisting in your daily 
training has paid off!

12:11.567 --> 12:13.357
Is it really that impressive?

12:12.327 --> 12:14.757
<i>Right. There's no need to rush.</i>

12:13.357 --> 12:16.657
As of this moment, it is assuredly 
Julie's greatest masterpiece!

12:15.227 --> 12:18.837
<i>I just need to keep chipping 
away, one stroke at a time.</i>

12:16.657 --> 12:19.767
Yeah? Now I'm curious to see 
her other works sometime.

12:19.767 --> 12:22.247
Of course! We'd love you to see them!

12:19.997 --> 12:21.467
<i>Alongside everybody else.</i>

12:22.247 --> 12:24.317
How about dinner at my place after this?

12:24.317 --> 12:26.877
Truly?! We wouldn't be intruding?

12:26.877 --> 12:29.987
Of course. I've been wanting 
to introduce you to Lucie.

12:29.987 --> 12:33.567
In that case, permit us to 
take you up on your offer.

12:33.567 --> 12:36.317
Thank you very much, Grand Master.

12:36.317 --> 12:39.177
Julie, be on your best behavior.

12:39.177 --> 12:40.697
Yes, Master!

12:41.267 --> 12:42.987
You don't want to do more tests?

12:42.987 --> 12:45.427
No. At least, not today.

12:45.757 --> 12:49.087
Would you mind helping again 
tomorrow, and in future?

12:50.557 --> 12:52.457
No problem. I'm your man!

12:54.557 --> 12:56.137
Thank you very much.

12:58.107 --> 13:04.047
<i>Okay. I'm making progress studying 
manatite and clearing the Sperd name.</i>

13:05.757 --> 13:08.097
<i>I'm getting along great with my family.</i>

13:08.567 --> 13:10.227
<i>Everything's coming up roses.</i>

13:13.937 --> 13:15.177
<i>Which means...</i>

13:15.577 --> 13:19.617
<i>it might finally be time to 
move on to the next step.</i>

13:22.707 --> 13:24.767
You don't mind, do you?

13:24.307 --> 13:26.157
No, I don't think—

13:24.767 --> 13:26.157
Pretty please?

13:26.157 --> 13:29.257
Just once. One time is enough for me.

13:28.577 --> 13:29.697
Hey.

13:29.257 --> 13:30.977
Please think it over.

13:30.977 --> 13:33.427
I'm sure we'll both 
get something out of it.

13:33.707 --> 13:36.927
I know you might not like the idea now,

13:36.927 --> 13:41.097
but I'm sure it will be better 
for both of us in the long run.

13:41.097 --> 13:43.957
Please say yes. I'm begging you.

13:41.657 --> 13:43.247
B-But still...

13:43.957 --> 13:44.917
This is the student council!

13:44.917 --> 13:47.037
Lord Luke!

13:44.927 --> 13:46.597
It's Silent Fitz!

13:46.597 --> 13:49.387
Fitz sure has gotten cuter lately.

13:47.037 --> 13:49.867
Lord Luke, you're always so dashing!

13:47.707 --> 13:49.047
Look over here!

13:49.387 --> 13:54.517
We received a report that you, Rudeus, 
were assaulting a female student.

13:57.787 --> 14:00.147
Fitz, you take it from here.

14:00.147 --> 14:01.117
Right.

14:01.557 --> 14:03.837
Clear out. Nothing to see here.

14:06.697 --> 14:09.597
A "female student," huh?

14:09.597 --> 14:11.247
You can't blame them.

14:11.247 --> 14:14.617
Word that you're a teacher 
probably hasn't gotten around yet.

14:14.867 --> 14:16.467
Listen, Rudy,

14:16.467 --> 14:19.637
I know you're married, 
but that's no excuse to force her.

14:19.637 --> 14:22.237
Sometimes girls just aren't in the mood.

14:22.237 --> 14:23.087
Huh?

14:23.087 --> 14:25.527
Yes, of course. I know that.

14:26.047 --> 14:31.647
I mean, maybe Roxy is better, 
but you do have me, too, so...

14:34.457 --> 14:36.017
Don't tell me...

14:40.147 --> 14:43.607
Oh, Sylphie! You're jealous!

14:43.607 --> 14:45.957
I w-wouldn't go quite that far.

14:45.957 --> 14:47.757
You have nothing to worry about, Sylphie.

14:47.757 --> 14:51.207
Of course I would never 
leave you out in the cold.

14:51.207 --> 14:52.697
Huh? But—

14:52.697 --> 14:54.597
You mean, all three of us?

14:54.597 --> 14:56.007
You bet.

14:56.007 --> 14:58.787
We'll get Roxy to teach us both at once.

15:00.257 --> 15:02.707
I haven't agreed to anything yet!

15:02.707 --> 15:04.657
Don't be like that.

15:04.657 --> 15:06.477
Sylphie, you want to learn, too, right?

15:07.027 --> 15:11.217
Um... Sorry, Rudy. 
What are you talking about?

15:11.517 --> 15:16.097
I asked Roxy to teach us 
king-class water magic.

15:21.147 --> 15:23.487
Matsukaze is a nice horse.

15:23.487 --> 15:27.787
He's obedient, docile, and strong, too.

15:27.787 --> 15:29.137
You're right about that.

15:29.137 --> 15:31.617
Horses like him are hard to find.

15:31.617 --> 15:33.887
Do you know a lot about horses?

15:33.887 --> 15:36.447
No, not really.

15:36.777 --> 15:41.677
But I have seen some of the best 
horses in the Asuran royal palace.

15:41.887 --> 15:44.207
The ones knight commanders 
and people like that ride.

15:44.207 --> 15:46.057
They must have been impressive.

15:47.417 --> 15:49.097
Oh, excuse me.

15:49.097 --> 15:51.157
You're impressive, too, of course.

15:51.157 --> 15:53.587
After all, you are the 
Greyrat family horse.

15:55.007 --> 15:57.907
Do you remember Caravaggio, Master?

15:57.907 --> 16:01.557
Yes. Paul's horse. 
That brings back memories.

16:01.557 --> 16:04.187
We rode out on horseback that time, too.

16:04.187 --> 16:06.267
Wait, which time?

16:06.267 --> 16:09.587
This was back when I was Rudy's tutor.

16:09.587 --> 16:13.377
I guess I hadn't met you yet then, had I?

16:13.377 --> 16:14.717
Oh, right.

16:15.277 --> 16:19.787
Come to think of it, this area 
does remind me a little of Buena.

16:20.027 --> 16:21.687
Now that you mention it...

16:21.687 --> 16:23.107
You may be right.

16:35.077 --> 16:37.767
<i>It's been an awfully long time since then.</i>

16:45.667 --> 16:48.967
Now that I've agreed to teach you, 
I'm going to do it properly.

16:49.407 --> 16:50.867
Are you ready?

16:51.167 --> 16:52.067
Yes.

16:52.067 --> 16:53.127
Go ahead.

16:54.867 --> 16:59.377
I'm going to cast the king-class 
water spell Lightning on that tree.

16:59.767 --> 17:01.497
Watch closely.

17:01.497 --> 17:02.477
Right.

17:09.197 --> 17:11.137
Well then, I'll begin.

17:12.627 --> 17:17.647
Grand spirit of water and imperial prince 
of lightning who ascends the heavens,

17:17.647 --> 17:21.247
grant my wish and bring 
about a savage blessing.

17:21.687 --> 17:24.517
Display your might to 
insignificant beings!

17:25.897 --> 17:29.217
Strike awe with a blow of your 
divine hammer on the anvil,

17:29.217 --> 17:31.187
and cover the land in water!

17:32.937 --> 17:38.327
Ah, Rain! Sweep all else 
away and expel everything!

17:33.307 --> 17:34.407
<i>Hang on.</i>

17:34.407 --> 17:36.737
<i>Isn't this Cumulonimbus?</i>

17:39.147 --> 17:44.157
Grand spirit of light and emperor 
of lightning who rules the heavens,

17:45.117 --> 17:46.497
<i>No, it's different.</i>

17:46.497 --> 17:48.507
can you see the one who 
stands tall, towering?!

17:48.807 --> 17:50.877
See Your Majesty's haughty foe?!

17:51.337 --> 17:56.317
I am one who would smite that 
foe with a divine blade!

17:56.317 --> 17:58.277
Bring your radiant might to bear

17:58.617 --> 18:00.757
and display your imperial majesty!

18:00.757 --> 18:02.297
Lightning!

18:15.037 --> 18:16.067
Whoa!

18:16.067 --> 18:17.517
Are you all right?

18:17.517 --> 18:19.687
I'm so glad it worked.

18:19.687 --> 18:24.087
Once is the limit with my mana, 
even using a wand.

18:24.087 --> 18:26.077
Anyway, did you see?

18:26.077 --> 18:27.467
Yes, Master.

18:27.957 --> 18:29.457
Do you think you can cast it?

18:29.817 --> 18:31.367
I'll try!

18:45.177 --> 18:49.827
Grand spirit of water and imperial prince 
of lightning who ascends the heavens,

18:49.827 --> 18:53.357
grant my wish and bring 
about a savage blessing.

18:53.357 --> 18:56.147
Display your might to 
insignificant beings.

18:59.527 --> 19:00.947
Wow...

18:59.857 --> 19:03.017
Strike awe with a blow of your 
divine hammer on the anvil,

19:03.017 --> 19:04.847
and cover the land in water!

19:05.167 --> 19:10.807
Ah, Rain! Sweep all else 
away and expel everything!

19:14.627 --> 19:18.877
Grand spirit of light and emperor 
of lightning who rules the heavens,

19:18.877 --> 19:21.237
can you see the one who 
stands tall, towering?!

19:21.237 --> 19:23.227
See Your Majesty's haughty foe?!

19:23.937 --> 19:29.007
I am one who would smite that 
foe with a divine blade!

19:29.007 --> 19:33.167
Bring your radiant might to bear 
and display your imperial majesty!

19:33.657 --> 19:34.907
Lightning!

20:03.887 --> 20:06.927
Now you're a king-class 
water mage, too, Rudy.

20:06.927 --> 20:08.817
It's kind of frustrating.

20:08.817 --> 20:11.447
How come I'm the only one 
who couldn't get it to work?

20:11.447 --> 20:14.747
Even I fail one time in five.

20:14.747 --> 20:18.537
Rudy did it on his first try. 
He really is something.

20:18.537 --> 20:22.337
True. I thought he might,

20:22.337 --> 20:25.927
but seeing him make it look 
easy still stings a little.

20:30.927 --> 20:32.277
It's beautiful.

20:32.277 --> 20:34.697
Yeah, it sure is.

20:35.377 --> 20:40.157
Lately, I find myself wondering 
if maybe I'm dreaming.

20:40.157 --> 20:41.257
Dreaming?

20:41.257 --> 20:42.097
Yes.

20:42.607 --> 20:45.607
Maybe I'm still in that labyrinth,

20:45.607 --> 20:49.037
having a happy dream 
on the verge of death.

20:49.777 --> 20:53.737
My life has gotten a lot nicer 
over the past six months.

20:54.137 --> 20:57.477
I was able to get married 
and become a teacher, too.

20:57.857 --> 21:01.557
You may see me as an interloper, Sylphie,

21:02.267 --> 21:07.637
but I'm glad that the three of us 
are able to ride together like this.

21:07.637 --> 21:10.867
You're not an "interloper."

21:10.867 --> 21:14.967
I'm glad to make friends with you, too.

21:14.967 --> 21:19.037
Especially since, if we fought 
over Rudy, I'd probably lose.

21:22.127 --> 21:24.887
In my case, I got lucky.

21:24.887 --> 21:29.677
I met Rudy again when he was in a 
bad place, and I managed to help him.

21:30.427 --> 21:34.397
He would never have given me 
a second glance otherwise.

21:34.697 --> 21:37.267
I'm pretty sure you're wrong about that.

21:37.267 --> 21:39.547
<i>I'm the lucky one.</i>

21:39.547 --> 21:43.097
<i>I could never have gone outside 
without Roxy to lead the way.</i>

21:43.097 --> 21:47.447
<i>I only have this happy life 
because Sylphie forgave me.</i>

21:47.837 --> 21:53.867
<i>Any promise I make to cherish them 
will probably come off as empty words.</i>

21:54.347 --> 21:57.167
<i>So, I'll let my actions speak for me.</i>

21:57.577 --> 22:01.187
<i>To protect them. To protect my family.</i>

22:01.927 --> 22:04.937
<b>Episode 4
A King-Class Water Mage</b>

23:34.937 --> 23:40.017
Next Time
Celebrations
